  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn a recent [cookie store PR](https://github.com/WICG/cookie-store/pull/256), we called into the \"[is a registrable domain suffix of or is equal to](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction)\".  Although this check internally runs the host parser for comparison, it unfortunately discards the parsed result, returning only a boolean (true or false). This necessitated re-running the host parser to store the parsed string, which is inefficient.\n\nIdeally, the check should return the parsed string directly, allowing callers to utilize the already computed result.\n\nCC: @annevk ",
